      {
        "id": 25917,
        "name": "TheJayMann",
        "username": "TheJayMann",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-02-03T13:13:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Per original ruling, if there were two Ongoing cards in play, each target would get hit for 1 fire damage + modifires twice (i.e. 2 + 2 fire damage if Staff of Ra is equipped).  If I’m not mistaken, new rulings with Rook City expansion will state that “for each” is enumerated for a grand total before applying modifires for a single attack, though that may have changed since I last spoke with Chris.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:59:48.818Z",
